{
  "rationale": "The plant automata model the robot's motion commands and perception outcomes as separate subsystems. The specification automata encode the safe and coverage-oriented exploration policy: always avoid collisions, recover conservatively, and maximize forward progress when possible. Obstacle events force recovery states with only safe actions enabled. After recovery, the robot returns to exploration as soon as the path is clear. Rotations are used for coverage and to avoid long runs in one direction.",
  "strategy": [
    "Separate plant automata for motion commands and perception outcomes to modularize sensing and actuation.",
    "Specification automata bind perception outcomes to safe, coverage-biased actions, enforce conservative recovery, and ensure transitions out of recovery as soon as the path is clear."
  ],
